WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.030
Speaking of moms, one of the biggest missions on our shows

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:06.730
is to keep moms feeling connected

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.430
and supported and heard, especially this year.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:11.340
My goodness.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.400
And you know, sometimes we just think,

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.590
how do we even take a break when you need it most?

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:19.750
And as a parent, you put yourself last.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.620
It's just a fact.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.780
And so we think about that here.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.130
And when a woman named Melissa reached out to us

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.160
about her friend, Angela,

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.680
we knew that we wanted to team up to surprise her

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.740
in a thing we like to call Mom's Time-out.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:40.200
Hey, Drew, I wanna nominate my girlfriend, Angela.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.440
She had cancer three or four years ago.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.150
And then, like six months later,

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.090
I was diagnosed with cancer as well.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.050
So we were both gone through breast cancer.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.030
She was my rock.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.380
She would come over and bring me cards

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.880
and leave little gifts on my doorstep.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:01.630
Angela lost her husband about nine years ago.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.690
And she had a four-year-old daughter

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.090
that she had to take care of.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.340
Whenever you see her, she just has that smile like that.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.330
Not only is she a single mother,

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.680
but she decided to foster kids herself.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.800
That's just the kind of person she is.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.050
And she'll go to our local restaurants and pick up soup

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.930
or pick up whatever food that they have.

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.150
And she delivers them all over.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:26.200
I mean, this girl is, she's crazy. (laughs)

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.160
I don't know where she finds the time to do that,

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:31.430
but it's so much a part of who she is.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:35.770
When I say Angela, I think of all the compassionate things

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.460
that she does for other people.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:40.350
And she never asked for anything for herself ever.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.900
She always puts people first,

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:45.281
and I think that is the most important thing.

00:01:45.281 --> 00:01:46.114
(audience applauding)

00:01:46.114 --> 00:01:47.520
Hi, Angela.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.120
I am so excited to meet you.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.410
How do you give back when you're being this example

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.283
of such an amazing person?

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.203
There's a variety of ways that I do give back.

00:02:03.069 --> 00:02:05.740
Me and a partner run a Christmas program

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:08.040
to where we help families in need,

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.720
make sure that they do not have,

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.620
that they aren't forgotten on Christmas.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.010
It's called Community Santa Project.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.760
I also help with my friends.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.510
Oh yes, there's the soup.

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.470
And Soup for Soul is one of the local restaurants.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:27.470
Donated soup to us, and we were able to get it to shelters,

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:31.253
as well as to local families in need.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:37.370
We also help with a local children's cancer organization

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:38.860
called Cancer Kiss my Cooley,

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.870
who was started by my best friends

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:44.890
after they lost their six-year-old to a brain tumor.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:49.460
So I have my spread out a little bit,

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:53.870
but just enough to give me balance while raising Kayla.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:58.130
Well, I would be honored if I could participate

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.930
in your Christmas program with my daughters,

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:04.490
because I'm always looking to find the road

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.480
to all the examples out there,

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.100
especially during the holidays.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.410
It's such a time where we're so aware

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:14.030
of how important it is to take care of each other.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:16.090
So we would love to put that on our website,

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:19.290
all of your missions on our website,

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:23.140
and help raise as much awareness and funds as we can.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.610
And you've been through so much

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.813
and lived such an extraordinary life.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:35.263
A couple examples is surviving cancer,

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.150
surviving the loss of a husband.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.510
Yes I did.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:46.510
And yet being able to be someone who really gives back

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.970
to their community through all of that.

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:54.653
May I ask how do you be the kind of person that you are?

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.750
I started out young.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:01.010
My parents were very giving and loving people.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.423
And I was raised that way.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.560
I want to be the best parent I can for my child,

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:11.810
and the way to do that is by leading by example.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.383
When I was pregnant with Olive, my first child,

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:21.050
I was scared of that notion, leading by example,

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:26.050
because my example was a very Bohemian self-sufficient life,

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:31.030
and I heard this story on none other than Oprah Radio.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:33.060
And Oprah said, "Gayle, Gayle, tell that story."

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:33.893
And she's like, "I don't know why

00:04:33.893 --> 00:04:35.040
you love this story so much."

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.760
And she's like, "Just tell it, just tell it."

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.750
And she's like, "I went and took my son Will to college,

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.790
and I noticed his dorm room fridge was empty.

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:45.940
And so I took him to the local store to get a few things,

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.410
and we noticed a traffic cop.

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.320
It was like the heat, summer.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.840
He was out there sweating, and we went in to get stuff,

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.680
and I came back and I saw him and I went back in.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.840
I got a case of water and I brought it to him.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.840
Why? Why do you love this story so much?"

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.050
And Oprah said, "Because in that moment,

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:05.740
you taught your son what kind of human being to be."

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.060
And it gave me the faith I needed,

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.470
as a mom with a baby in my belly,

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:15.000
that examples were true and that they do work.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.740
But never in a million years

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:22.570
can you really hold someone up higher than you.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:25.030
Thank you, Drew. Thank you.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:28.020
Angela, I have a confession actually.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:31.100
Your best friend, Melissa, actually reached out to me,

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.520
and she's here with us today.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:33.692
Hi Melissa.

00:05:33.692 --> 00:05:34.694
(audience cheering)

00:05:34.694 --> 00:05:35.611
Hi, guys.

00:05:38.214 --> 00:05:39.854
Hi, Angie!

00:05:39.854 --> 00:05:41.021
Hi, Melissa.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.880
Melissa, did you want to tell Angela something today?

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.540
Oh god, I'm gonna start crying.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:50.710
You know how much you mean to me

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:52.570
and everything that you have gone through.

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:55.610
And you're always putting everybody first.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:58.830
When I was diagnosed, you were first person to call me

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.500
and like, "What do you need?

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.897
I'm there for you."

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:05.470
That meant a lot, obviously,

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:06.960
because you knew what I was going through,

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.403
going through it yourself.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:13.183
Just watching you, oh, okay, I'm gonna start crying.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.380
You mean so much to me.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.273
And I hope that you know that.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.440
I do.
Sorry I'm emotional.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.683
It is such a beautiful thing.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.440
Really I'm just here to say,

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:33.360
we wanted to celebrate all the amazing work

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.020
that you have done for your community.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.460
And we'd love to treat you

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:41.130
to an all-expense-paid vacation to Fiji for two.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.342
I hope that would be okay.

00:06:43.342 --> 00:06:45.475
Oh my goodness, that would be wonderful.

00:06:45.475 --> 00:06:46.880
Okay, great.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.090
And when it's safe to travel again,

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.700
we're gonna send you and a guest

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:54.780
to Yasawa Island Resort and Spa, Fiji,

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:58.570
which is tucked away off the coast of Fiji's main island,

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:02.350
and they offer the ultimate in all-inclusive luxury.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:04.130
And you'll be arriving courtesy

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:07.230
of the national airline of Fiji, Fiji Airways.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.880
And by the way, those airlines are like having

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.080
a trip in itself.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.470
And so from when the car picks you up

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:17.060
to the very last minute of your vacation,

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.160
we're just gonna take care of the whole thing

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.880
and make sure it is nearly as perfect as you are.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:25.920
So this is our way of saying thank you again

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.790
for being an example

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:30.970
and the exceptional person that you are.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:33.830
This is a well-deserved Mom's Time-out.

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:37.410
Oh, that's so amazing. Thank you so much, Drew.

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:39.210
Thank you, Angela and Melissa.

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:41.512
Thanks for letting me hang out with you guys.

00:07:41.512 --> 00:07:44.095
(upbeat music)

